Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||01-02-2001||02:51 PM||||Hi,  I was reading through the archives on the subject of targa tops.  I saw that a few people have actually done exactly what I've been thinking for years.  Making the center section of the roof removable, and beefing up the frame to compensate for the structural change.  I was just wandering if any of those who have done it could comment on how it's working out or give any advice to me on how to do this.  I would like to have my Fiero targa topped by summer.  Pictures would be great also!<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike Schaefer<BR>Worldwide Fiero Links <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-02-2001||07:17 PM||||You should email John Norman (owner/builder of Obsession).  He did a targa very successfully.  He did a partial tube frame type reinforcement and has a Pro Street style roll cage in the cockpit.  Makes ingress/egress slightly more difficult, but I'll bet everything's still tight in 10 years.||||reg||1
