Z||000006||MikeSchaefer||01-03-2001||09:17 PM||||Could you post the general steps in completing the process?  What problems have you had (if any?).  What is the total amount of $ and time you have invested in the conversion?  Sorry for all of the questions, but I'm very interested.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||80's BOY||01-03-2001||09:45 PM||||where to start....<BR>assuming you read my other posts and did a search on this topic, i'll go from there. you can reply with specific questions after i give the basics.<P>basically i jacked up the car from the center of the vehicle on both sides with floor jacks, and cut the roof out. first the fiberglass, then the space frame. then i welded in some pipe at an angle from the floorboard up to behind the mid-seat section where the seatbelt sticks out of the plastic. (i did document all this for measurements, i'm just stuck at work right now). so i have a partial roll-bar lookalike  with nice padded covers at a low angle right when you open the doors. not all people will want this in the way so under-the-frame strengthening might be what you're thinking. capped off the header with sunbird convertible parts, and for the rear, a modified piece of roof panel from a parts car to cap off the ugliness, along with t-top "B" post covers from fierottop.com (i think). i still have to work on three things..<P>1) how to attach a headliner i like without making it look too cheesy.<P>2) minor complications on re-attachment of targa.i have never driven the car with the top on since i cut out the top, and probably never will. weekend car.<P>3)window seals, but again my car never sees the rain either.<P>sorry so long.<P>Brian O<P>squirrellsack@yahoo.com<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||MikeSchaefer||01-04-2001||12:20 PM||||80's boy:  I'd love to see the pictures you have, especially pictures of the bar you built.  <BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike||||reg||6
